WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Compression shortens layered rock. When conditions favor ductile deformation,

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.120
layers bend. Watch the beds and their boundaries change

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.520
shape together. An upright arch with older layers in

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.800
its core is an anticline. A trough with younger

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.060
central layers is a syncline. A step-like bend is

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:21.300
a monocline. Ages matter when later deformation overturns layers.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.060
Limbs meet near a hinge. An axial surface connects

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.540
hinges through successive layers. Tilt that surface to make

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.700
an inclined fold. A plunging axis slopes into the

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.940
ground, changing the map pattern. Describe geometry before inferring

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:36.220
history.
